{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>But the Levites by their fathers' tribe were not counted among them</b> – Now at the outset Moses decided on his own not to count the Levites, because it was said to him (Numbers 1:4), \"With you shall be, each man, for his tribe,\" etc., for all the tribes that were counted would have their princes. And since he did not appoint a prince from the children of Levi, he did not count them. Now Moses was in doubt concerning the matter of the Levites and did not know what to do with them, and when he had completed the entire count of the people and only the Levites alone remained, the Holy One, blessed be He, made it known to him that he should not count them among the children of Israel, but should count them separately, for He would appoint them over the Tabernacle of the Testimony. And He said (Numbers 3:14), \"Count the children of Levi\" — that he should count them by himself alone, without the princes, and he called Aaron to be with him, for he is the prince of that tribe; and just as the princes of Israel were with their tribes, so would the prince of the Levites be among them. And perhaps this is the reason for the vowel point on \"and Aaron\" (ibid. v. 39), for it was not explicitly by the word of YHWH. Afterward, in the counting of the Levites for their service and their burden, Moses called the princes of the congregation to be with him, as it is said (Numbers 4:46), \"whom Moses and Aaron and the princes of Israel counted, the Levites,\" for it is fitting that they all agree and see to the arrangement of the watches. And there too he again said in another place (below 4:37, 45), \"whom Moses and Aaron counted by the word of YHWH, by the hand of Moses,\" for he had already hinted by means of the vowel point that Aaron was with him by obligation — for Moses saw fit to do so — while the princes of the congregation were optional, for Moses called them to conduct himself toward them with honor. And in tractate Bekhorot (Bekhorot 4a) they said that the vowel point on Aaron is to hint that he was not included in the counting of the Levites at all."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Bekhorot 4a; the folio reference is correct. The verse citations from Numbers 3 and 4 have been normalized to standard chapter:verse format. The phrase 'the Holy One, blessed be He' renders הקב״ה, a standard reverential abbreviation not subject to the divine-name transliteration rule."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:17.203759594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}